From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:59:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 514/514] [DS4.1] Sparse-MLA metadata builders: requests and
 tokens in one launch

Every KV-cache group's builder launched the request metadata and the token
metadata as two eager kernels before each step's graph: 26 groups at a
DS4.1 decode step (23 target, 3 drafter), so 52 launches, half of them
one 1.2 us CTA of request starts, positions and counts. The two parts read
only the step's inputs, never each other's outputs.

builder_kernel writes both in one launch, the request blocks first, with
the same arithmetic as the two kernels; requests_kernel and tokens_kernel
are gone. Profiled ceiling (request inventory 5, TP4 ring, rank 0): the
request kernels are 0.09% of a c1 decode step's device time and 0.07% at
c8, plus 26 TileLang launches of host time in each step's preparation.

Tests: one launch writes the torch references' request and token
metadata exactly, over the packed steps and the paged and ring geometries
the pair's tests used.
benchmark_deepseek_v41_metadata_builder.py times it against the two
kernels (kept as they were at 26382f5cf), eagerly with the host's launch
cost and under graphs, gated.
